<title>CANADA: CBRS upgrades New Brunswick ratings,outlook stable.</title>
<headline>CBRS upgrades New Brunswick ratings,outlook stable.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Bond Rating Service said on Friday that it had upgraded New Brunswick's short-term debt rating to A-1+ from A-1 and the province's long-term debt rating to A+ from A.</p>
<p>CBRS said the rating outlook on New Brunswick's paper was stable.</p>
<p>&quot;The combination of good economic performance and reductions in expenditures, sales and income taxes, and net debt has contributed to the rating upgrade,&quot; CBRS said.</p>
<p>&quot;Barring a significant economic downturn, New Brunswick's economic and fiscal performance should continue to strengthen over the next few years,&quot; CBRS added.</p>
<p>((Paul Simao, Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8104))</p>
